{#
    A spend figure, per currency, with the combined total when there is an
    honest one to show.

    One currency is one line — the design's clean number, and the common case.
    Several that all convert are the combined figure with the subtotals beneath
    it. Several where one has no rate are the subtotals and no total at all,
    because a headline that silently omits a currency is a wrong number rather
    than an approximate one.

    Shared by the dashboard's spend tiles and the my-subscriptions strip. The
    rule is the same on both screens, so it is written once: two copies of it
    would eventually be two rules.

    `figures.estimate_currencies` names the currencies that hold a bill whose
    amount varies: their subtotals, and the combined figure, are drawn "≈"
    (`partials/estimate.twig`). A currency of fixed rows only is not.
#}
{% macro spend(figures, unit) %}
    {% import 'partials/estimate.twig' as estimate %}
    {% if figures.totals is empty %}
        <p class="stat-value num">{{ t('common.none_symbol') }}</p>
        <p class="muted">{{ t('dashboard.recurring_empty') }}</p>
    {% elseif figures.totals|length == 1 %}
        <p class="stat-value num">
            {{ estimate.mark(figures, figures.totals[0].amount_minor|money(figures.totals[0].currency), figures.totals[0].currency) }}
            <span class="stat-unit num">{{ unit }}</span>
        </p>
    {% elseif figures.combined.amount_minor is not null %}
        <p class="stat-value num">
            {{ estimate.mark(figures, figures.combined.amount_minor|money(figures.combined.currency)) }}
            <span class="stat-unit num">{{ unit }}</span>
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
            {% for total in figures.totals %}
                {{ estimate.mark(figures, total.amount_minor|money(total.currency), total.currency) }}{{ not loop.last ? ' · ' : '' }}
            {% endfor %}
        </p>
    {% else %}
        {# No rate for one of them, so there is no total — only the subtotals. #}
        <ul class="plain stat-lines">
            {% for total in figures.totals %}
                <li class="stat-value stat-line num">{{ estimate.mark(figures, total.amount_minor|money(total.currency), total.currency) }}</li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>
        <p class="hint">
            {{ t('dashboard.unconvertible', {
                'currencies': figures.combined.unconvertible|join(', '),
            }) }}
        </p>
    {% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
